- Added Google conditional access device registration (Fleet Premium): company-owned iOS and iPadOS hosts sign in to Google through fleetdm.com, company-owned Android hosts are registered automatically after enrollment with no sign-in, and Fleet stores the host's Google device users and marks them as managed with the customer's service account. Added the device status route, the `POST /api/v1/fleet/google_conditional_access/register` route that fleetdm.com calls, and a cron that registers Android hosts, unmarks hosts deleted or unenrolled from Fleet, retries failed marks, and marks hosts registered with the Google bookmark flow.
- Changed `PUT /api/v1/fleet/hosts/:id/google_device_id` to require Google conditional access to be connected and a company-owned host, and to mark the device's users as managed in Google. `DELETE /api/v1/fleet/hosts/:id/google_device_id` now also unmarks them. A host's `google_device_id` is also set when its end user signs in to Google (iOS and iPadOS) or when Fleet registers it (Android).
